                        "glosses": [
                            "Someone who rides a donkey."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "41b57365-3d21-431d-b95c-eca9a6dc8960",
                                "sense_id": "d31c80ed-d738-3645-8a86-69f5562ea628",
                                "text": "1856, Emmeline Stuart-Wortley, The Sweet South, London: Printed for Private Circulation: Volume 2, Chapter 14, p. 173,\nWe met several camelestrians on our road, and horsemen and assmen; and the scenery in many parts was very pretty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d6923fb-cf9c-46aa-afb5-a53eef9d2158",
                                "sense_id": "d31c80ed-d738-3645-8a86-69f5562ea628",
                                "text": "No sooner was Tom upright than the donkey gave the whole of his skin and muscles a wrench sidewise, which felt as if the seat was being dragged away. ¶ The consequence was that Tom nearly went off to the right. He was too good an assman, though […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ded6960-2ba8-4663-a1a4-8954e951d60a",
                                "sense_id": "d31c80ed-d738-3645-8a86-69f5562ea628",
                                "text": "Even the asses have a fashionable air, large white beasts loaded with cushions, fringes, and tassels; so that horsemen and assmen trot side by side on equal terms in the gay parade."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
